Read the kde-gtk-config colour names in the GTK theme

No rule of the four sheets read a name that kde-gtk-config writes, so a
sheet alone could not follow a colour change. A name now moves the sheets
with no run of the writer.

The emitter derives a shade step, a gradient stop and a role alpha from a
colour name with shade(), mix() and alpha(). GTK shade() computes the HSL
model alone, so a literal ships under the other three models. 308 of the 324
GTK 3 declarations with a colour read a name. 132 of the 134 :root entries
with a colour read one of 24 names.

A caption follows the colour scheme only over a ground that follows it. It
then reads the foreground name of the colour group of that ground, because a
user colour file moves one group at a time. The writer gives exit code 5 to
a cross group pair and to a mix of two groups. 105 new rules of the GTK 3
sheet follow a name, and 108 of the GTK 4 one. 155 declarations of a shared
selector changed from a literal to a name.

Neither dialect held a rule for a selected span of text, which now takes the
selection pair over 12 selectors. A selected span of a window that is not
active takes the two inactive selection names.

A popup menu grounds on the window colour and pairs it with the window
foreground, which both references paint. A selected row that the user cannot
use loses the selection ground. An accent button, a plain button and a
window label paint a cue of a state that showed none.

paths.txt binds every caption, ground, ink and derived line, alphas.txt
every translucent value, and shades.txt every shade factor.

The change sits on the branch work/gtk4-theme of the local tree. The push puts
that branch on the fork wyn/qtcurve. The merge request on system/qtcurve
follows that push.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

